# Docstring standard

When creating or editing a function, class, or module in matching files, follow
`.cursor/skills/docstrings/SKILL.md`.

Every public item must document: purpose, parameters (meaning + types), return
value, raises, and limits/upper–lower bounds where numeric or sized. Domain
code must note side effects (stock, wallet, audit, journals).

Same standard applies to **existing** public APIs when a module is under a
documentation pass — do not leave thin one-liners on services/models you touch.

Update `docs/modules/<app>.md` when documenting or introducing a Django app.
